messages:
Maya (Content): Hey team — new draft of the launch blog is up for a short pass. Link: https://notion.so/redwood/launch-v3-draft

Owen (Growth): read through. Love the flow but let's be explicit about which hardware + batch settings in the benchmark callout so customers can reproduce. Suggest a one-line: 'Benchmarks executed on g5.12xlarge with steady-state batching (batch size 16) — see repo for raw logs.'

Sofia (Design): fig-2 missing alt text. Recommend alt: 'Throughput and median latency by sequence length'. Also suggest a compact benchmark card under the hero so the key metric is visible without scrolling.

Ravi (Sales Ops): CTA split required: Start trial (self-serve) and Request enterprise demo. Demo form must capture arr_band, deployment_preference, and account_region as hidden fields. Enterprise leads route to Sales Queue D. SLA: touch within 1 business day.

Claire (Legal): flag: phrase '40% lower inference cost' needs documentation. Please either cite internal cost appendix or soften to 'lower inferred per-token costs in our tests' until finance signs off. Also ensure any customer quotes are approved in writing.

Maya (Content): will soften cost language and add footnote pointing to internal appendix access. Also moving benchmark card above the fold and compressing the hero to one sentence. Will add a short methodology line.

devrel-bot: Suggestion: include a reproducer snippet in appendix showing prompt, model config, and exact CLI commands. Small code excerpt increases trust.

Owen (Growth): webinar teaser under CTAs please: one line + registration link. Proposed: 'Live launch webinar May 15 — benchmark walkthrough + rollout patterns. Register: https://events.redwood.ai/may15'

Sofia (Design): also request we inline a tiny svg summary for social sharing. Keeps visuals consistent.

Ravi (Sales Ops): HubSpot embed sample (please paste into blog form):
```
// HubSpot embed example for launch blog
const hubspotConfig = {
  formId: "form_trial" || "form_ent_demo",
  hiddenFields: {
    utm_source: "launch_blog",
    utm_medium: "blog",
    utm_campaign: "spring_launch",
    arr_band: "${arr_band}",
    deployment_preference: "${deployment_pref}",
    account_region: "${region}"
  }
};
```

Claire (Legal): also confirm we avoid direct competitor names unless we have explicit citations. Good to see the softer copy.

publish-bot: Checklist update: awaiting signoff from Legal and Sales Ops to enable enterprise routing. Target publish: 2024-05-10T09:00:00-07:00 (PT). Webinar tentative: 2024-05-15T11:00:00-07:00 (PT). :hourglass:

Maya (Content): final asks — can someone add the reproducer + one small graph to the appendix? DevRel, can you attach the repo link and a short run command?

devrel-bot: Repo link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/launch-bench; suggested run: `python run_bench.py --model redwood-llama-7b --batch-size 16 --seq-len 512 --runs 10` — I'll add a tiny results table.

Owen (Growth): GA tracking snippet for CTA clicks (please add before publish):
```
document.querySelectorAll('.launch-cta').forEach(btn => {
  btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    gtag('event','launch_cta_click',{event_label: btn.dataset.cta});
  });
});
```

Sofia (Design): I'll add alt text and prepare the share SVG.

Ravi (Sales Ops): I'll validate HubSpot form IDs and routing rules today and confirm assignment rules for queue D.

Claire (Legal): I'll review the softened cost phrasing and the quote approvals doc.

Maya (Content): I'll push the updated draft in ~40 minutes with the compressed hero, benchmark card above fold, alt text, HubSpot embed, and blurred cost language. If no objections by EOD, schedule publish for May 10 09:00 PT.

publish-bot: Reminder scheduled: final publish checklist runs 24 hours before target.

Maya (Content): thanks all — closing thread when updated draft is posted.
